WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.040
Not all Hulk battles are equal.

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.340
While some are thrilling, some do a disservice
to the strongest Avenger.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.240
But almost all give us plenty of smashing.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:11.500
From one-on-one gladiator matches to the big
guy facing a whole horde of baddies, here's

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.660
our picks for all the Hulk's MCU fights from
worst to best.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.400
If you've never heard of the Worf Effect,
it's simple you take the biggest, toughest

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.860
good guy, and you have the bad guy beat the
tar out of him right out of the gate.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.700
That way, your audience knows the villain
means business.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.440
This is exactly what happens in the opening
minutes of 2018's Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.800
The Hulk attacks Thanos, only to get easily
beaten unconscious by the Mad Titan.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.380
Even if you forget the fact that this makes
no sense when we consider how well less powerful

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.940
heroes like Captain America fare against Thanos,
the Hulk/Thanos bout works hard to earn its

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.000
lousy spot on our list because the green guy
never gets his shot at a rematch.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.500
Worse still, we hardly see him at all in the
final battle of 2019's Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.820
Treating the Hulk to a taste of the Worf Effect
is bad.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:59.399
Making it his last major action scene in the
MCU's decade-long Infinity Saga?

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.400
That's pretty unforgivable.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.480
Avengers: Age of Ultron opens with the team
reunited and raiding a Hydra base in Eastern

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:05.980
Europe.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.580
We don't see a lot of the Hulk during the
fight compared to some of the other heroes,

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.380
but what we do see is definitely impressive.

00:01:11.909 --> 00:01:15.479
Among other things, we get to see the Hulk
plow into the Hydra bunker threatening Hawkeye

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.240
and Black Widow and walk through it like it
isn't even there.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:22.140
We also get some great shots of the Hulk,
including during our introduction to Black

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:25.280
Widow's technique of effecting the Hulk's
transformation back to Bruce Banner.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:31.520
In 2017's Thor: Ragnarok, Thor has Loki unleash
the fire giant Surtur, who fulfills his destiny

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.220
by destroying Asgard and the villain Hela
in the process.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.920
"You can't defeat me."

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.100
“ No, I know.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.800
But he can."

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:48.020
As Surtur demolishes the Golden Realm, the
Hulk returns from his fight with Fenris the

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.040
wolf, and no one's bothered to tell him the
plan.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.940
So the Hulk does what the Hulk does he smashes.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.780
Or, at least, he tries.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.240
Once Hulk lands on the Bifrost, Thor manages
to stop him from attacking Surtur again.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.240
It's one of a bunch of funny moments the Thor/Hulk
odd couple enjoys in Ragnarok.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.780
As good as it is, we have to admit there was
some disappointment, especially since the

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.880
Hulk leaping at Surtur was used prominently
in Ragnarok's trailers.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.440
It's a great gag, but you can hardly be blamed
if you were primed for a full-length world-shattering

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:16.080
clash.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.080
While the other "Revengers" clash with Hela
and her undead army in Thor: Ragnarok, the

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:21.940
Hulk has another job.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:26.500
The green Goliath goes one-on-one with Hela's
favorite pet, the giant wolf Fenris.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.000
Their battle has them topple off the Bifrost
and into the water below.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.200
Fenris gives the Hulk a good fight, biting
deep into his emerald hide at one point and

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:38.700
thrashing him around underwater, but the Hulk
gives his canine foe one last massive punch

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.700
that sends the beast falling into the void.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.700
It's a good fight, though it feels like we
don't really get enough of it.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.560
There are shots of it here and there in between
the battle on the Bifrost.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.800
Honestly though, it seems like they only bothered
with putting Fenris in this movie at all so

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.440
the Hulk had something to do at the end while
everyone else was busy with character development.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.440
The battle between the poor S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.800
pilot who opens fire on the Hulk during the
man-monster's Helicarrier rampage in the first

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:05.420
Avengers film isn't much of a battle but it's
scary, funny, and it tells us a lot about

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:06.220
the Hulk early on.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.340
Maria Hill orders the pilot to engage the
Hulk, and when he opens fire, the big guy

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:11.380
just gets mad.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:13.720
"Target angry Target angry!"

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:19.410
Remember, this was the first "Hulk out" sequence
since 2008, and it lets us know right away

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:23.430
Joss Whedon intends for his version of the
Hulk to be much more powerful than the one

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:24.320
in the earlier film.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.700
The very fact that he's able to survive the
explosion of the jet and the subsequent drop

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.540
makes him seem much more powerful than the
Hulk of the 2008 movie.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:36.160
Bruce Banner doesn't want the Other Guy to
get involved in the final battle of Avengers:

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.870
Age of Ultron, but when Black Widow pushes
him off a ledge, she doesn't give him much

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:40.580
of a choice.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.400
Once he and Widow are on the floating island
that Sokovia has become along with the rest

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.840
of the team, Nat tells him to "go be a hero,"
and he does.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:50.400
At first, we don't really get to see much
of it.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.330
We only get a couple shots of Hulk stomping
Ultron's drones before the villain's final

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.020
assault on the team at the center of town.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:00.460
But that's when the Hulk gets really busy
with the robot smashing, even destroying robots

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.260
with his teeth.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:06.180
And of course, after Vision, Iron Man, and
Thor turn Ultron into mostly melted slag,

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.500
the green guy shows up to give him a punch
that sends him flying for miles.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.900
As soon as the Hulk's attack on Black Widow
is interrupted in The Avengers, and it was

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.920
revealed her savior was Thor, any old school
Marvel fan had to be excited.

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:21.600
Who wouldn't be up for a bout between these
two heavy hitters with technology that could

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:27.100
finally do it justice, unlike the cringe-worthy
battle in 1988's The Incredible Hulk Returns.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.740
This fight has some great moments, with perhaps
the most memorable being Thor's epic hammer

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:35.199
shot to Hulk's face,and the Hulk's failed
attempt to lift Mjolnir.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:39.099
For the most part, Hulk dominates the thunder
god during their first match, but the two

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:42.400
don't really have the room on the Helicarrier
to truly let loose like they could.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.619
Not counting the brief flashback montage in
the beginning of 2008's The Incredible Hulk,

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.880
our first true "Hulk out" scene in the MCU
is when Bruce Banner is cornered by his hostile

00:04:51.889 --> 00:04:55.949
coworkers in the Brazilian bottling plant
while he's trying to escape the Black Ops

00:04:55.949 --> 00:04:57.060
team led by Emil Blonsky.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.880
This scene feels more like something out of
a horror movie.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:04.300
We watch Hulk mercilessly bludgeoning the
soldiers with his bare green fists, mostly

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.440
without us seeing more than shadows of the
beast.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.760
It makes it that much more powerful when he
finally reveals himself to Blonsky, seconds

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.400
before hurling a forklift at him.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.800
"Yes!"

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:26.100
The gladiator battle between Hulk and Thor
in Thor: Ragnarok is classic.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:30.580
It's beautiful to look at it, it's funny with
callbacks to Natasha's lullaby and Loki's

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:34.680
epic beatdown in The Avengers, and it gives
these two powerhouses the chance to really

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:35.400
cut loose.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:39.460
It would get a higher spot on our list, except
that it really doesn't make any sense.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:44.509
Plot-wise, the battle serves mainly to introduce
us to Thor's new Raiden-esque lightning abilities,

00:05:44.509 --> 00:05:48.140
and in order to get there, the scene breaks
from everything we've seen in the MCU up until

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:48.640
now.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.840
The Hulk utterly dominates Thor in their battle
on the Helicarrier in The Avengers, and the

00:05:52.849 --> 00:05:57.029
only time Thor manages to get the edge is
when he summons Mjolnir ... which is shattered

00:05:57.029 --> 00:05:59.700
on a cliff in Norway at the time of his Sakaar
battle with Hulk.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:04.270
From what we've seen of the combatants' respective
strength and stamina in past battles, Thor

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:07.669
shouldn't even last to the point where he
gets his vision of power from Odin.

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:10.220
It's a fun battle, but it would be more fun
if it made sense.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:15.040
Yes, it's a bit of a stretch to call Hulk's
sucker punch of Thor in The Avengers a "fight,"

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:15.540
but c'mon.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:16.580
It's hilarious.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.500
It's also a perfect character moment.

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.300
The Hulk doesn't play well with others.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:24.550
Thor may be on his side at the time being,
but to the Hulk, that doesn't make them friends.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.620
It makes Thor someone he's not currently smashing
... much.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.340
He's had plenty of fights with others, but
so far, the MCU has given us exactly one big

00:06:32.349 --> 00:06:36.360
knock-down clash between the Hulk and one
of his most dangerous villains: the Abomination,

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:40.300
who throws down with the Green Goliath at
the end of 2008's Incredible Hulk.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:44.389
If you forgive that movie for its failings,
you can see that final brawl as one of the

00:06:44.389 --> 00:06:46.260
all-time great superhero clashes.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:50.500
The Abomination starts off stronger than the
hero, but as the fight progresses and the

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:54.020
Hulk keeps getting angrier, the Hulk's increasing
strength puts him over the edge.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:58.540
At the end, we get the Hulk uttering his famous
catchphrase for the first time onscreen, and

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:00.280
dare we say it, it's… smashing.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.740
In the comics, the Hulk's most persistent
foe isn't a supervillain, it's the United

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:08.080
States military, led by General Thaddeus "Thunderbolt"
Ross.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:12.050
The Incredible Hulk gave us a great example
of this conflict when the army corners Bruce

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:16.220
Banner on a college campus, forcing him to
Hulk out and smash his way through them.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:17.760
And smash he does.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:21.740
While this Hulk doesn't express quite as much
physical power as later versions, the battle

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.540
does a good job showing us exactly what he's
capable of.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:28.970
He's merely annoyed by the bullets, and even
Tony Stark's sonic weapons just increase his

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:30.880
rage when he sees Betty in distress.

00:07:31.429 --> 00:07:36.260
We also get a kind of preview of Captain America
when pre-Abomination Emil Blonsky makes the

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:40.580
bad choice of trying to take the Hulk on solo
with his new super solider abilities, and

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.800
gets punted into a tree for his troubles.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:47.360
The Hulk's epic domination of Loki at the
end of The Avengers is an absolute landmark

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.439
in the Infinity Saga.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.620
It is, first and foremost, one of the funniest
scenes in the MCU.

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.020
The comedy is the main reason the scene is
so memorable, but it actually provides a perfect

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.820
climax to one of the film's themes.

00:07:58.189 --> 00:08:01.920
Throughout The Avengers, we're hearing from
less "super" characters like Nick Fury who

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:05.360
are talking about how the world is struggling
to react to all of these thunder gods and

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.780
unfrozen super soldiers who are suddenly showing
up.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.839
The Hulk's abrupt and merciless thrashing
of Loki is the perfect reflection of what

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.100
Nick Fury is talking about.

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:17.600
Not only have these heroes become people who
"can't be matched" by ordinary humans, not

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:20.660
even an arrogant alien calling himself a god
can compare to them.

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:23.520
"Puny god."

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:33.580
A lot of people had a lot of problems with
2015's Avengers: Age of Ultron, but the Hulk's

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:38.409
battle with Tony Stark's Hulkbuster suit,
aka "Veronica," is a stunning, epic battle

00:08:38.409 --> 00:08:41.360
and one of the high action marks of the Marvel
Cinematic Universe.

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:45.819
While the idea that Tony Stark has armor designed
specifically to take down the Hulk is lifted

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:50.180
straight from the comics, the filmmakers add
some wonderful touches that make perfect sense.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:54.209
For example, there's the fact that Stark has
to keep the suit in orbit while he isn't using

00:08:54.209 --> 00:08:56.220
it so he can call upon it whenever he needs
it.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:59.800
And then there are all the cool features,
like being able to turn one of the suit's

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:04.060
fists into a trap that grabs the Hulk's wrist
and stops him from hurting anyone else.

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:08.149
While he doesn't win, the Hulk makes a good
showing, and Tony's apology when he realizes

00:09:08.149 --> 00:09:09.420
how mad his opponent is?

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:11.820
That's one of the MCU's most perfect moments.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:17.660
"I'm sorry."

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:25.500
While 2012's The Avengers brought together
heroes from all over the Marvel Cinematic

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:29.750
Universe, the Hulk stole the show in the final
battle against Loki's Chitauri army in New

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:30.400
York City.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:34.180
He tears through the Chitauri foot soldiers
easily, and he's the character at the heart

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:37.880
of one of the MCU's most classic, memorable,
and satisfying scenes.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:43.960
"That's my secret, I'm always angry."

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:51.760
It not only shows us how staggeringly powerful
the Hulk is, but it's a great character moment

00:09:51.769 --> 00:09:56.050
as well, serving as the final ingredient the
Avengers need to go from being a ragtag group

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.960
of superheroes to an actual team.

